* sky130-gcedram -- 2T-min bitcell transient write / read / hold testbench
* Issue #27 (gap-to-T1 tracker #13, items 5 and 9). First circuit-level
* simulation of the ratified 2T gain-cell bitcell: the leakage deck in
* sim/leakage/ is a DC operating point on a single access device, and
* sim/retention/ is an analytic derivation -- neither exercises the cell
* as a circuit. See sim/bitcell-transient/README.md for the full writeup,
* the rationale behind every timing/bias choice below, and the
* cross-check against the analytic retention numbers.
*
* THE DESIGN UNDER TEST IS INCLUDED, NOT TRANSCRIBED. The two devices
* come from design/gain_cell_2t.spice -- the netlist derived from
* design/gain_cell_2t.sch by design/regen_netlist.sh -- included verbatim
* below. Nothing in this deck restates the devices, their sizing, or
* their connectivity, so a schematic change propagates here through
* regen_netlist.sh rather than through a hand edit. The included netlist
* declares `.GLOBAL GND`; ngspice aliases the node name `gnd` to node 0,
* so the device bodies land on the testbench ground with no extra source.
* (design/gain_cell_2t.spice ends with `.end`; ngspice does not treat a
* `.end` inside an included file as the end of the parent deck, verified
* against ngspice-46 -- the sources below are parsed after the include.)
*
* Cell under test (from design/README.md "Topology"), both devices
* sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 W=0.42 um L=0.15 um:
*   M_WR  gate=wl   drain=sn   source=bl   body=GND   (write access)
*   M_RD  gate=sn   drain=rbl  source=rwl  body=GND   (read)
*
* READ-SELECT POLARITY (a design decision this deck records, not invents).
* `rwl` idles at VDD and a read pulls it LOW (active-low read select),
* sensing the resulting current on `rbl`, held at VRBL = VDD/2. For a
* DESELECTED row, `rbl` (not `rwl`) is the lower-voltage terminal, so
* BSIM4 swaps M_RD's effective source/drain to make `rbl` the effective
* source: the deselect bias is Vgs(M_RD) = V(sn) - V(rbl), which is
* SUBTHRESHOLD but not off for a stored '1' (e.g. +0.32 V at sf/125 C) --
* i_rbl_deselect_a measures exactly that residual. The alternative, `rwl`
* idling LOW, is worse: `rbl` then stays the effective drain, so the bias
* is the full Vgs(M_RD) = V(sn), which conducts far harder. Both
* wordlines still swing 0 V / VDD only -- no boosted level -- per
* design/README.md "Wordline drive scheme: plain 1.8 V (not boosted)".
* See the README's "Read scheme" section for the full derivation.
*
* THREE PHASES, ONE .tran (times are the .param values below):
*   1. WRITE  wl pulses 0 -> VDD -> 0 with bl held at the data level for
*      the whole pulse; bl returns to 0 only AFTER wl is fully low, so the
*      cell is never written by a bitline transition. V(sn) is recorded at
*      TWL_OFF (the instant the wordline fall begins -- the write ceiling)
*      and again after the fall (the level actually retained, after
*      wordline-to-storage-node feedthrough).
*   2. READ   rwl pulses VDD -> 0 -> VDD with rbl held at VRBL through
*      vrbl, whose branch current IS the read current. The deselected-row
*      current on rbl is sampled just before the read pulse.
*   3. HOLD   wl = 0, bl = 0, rwl = VDD, rbl = VRBL -- the same bias the
*      DC leakage deck (sim/leakage/tb_access_leakage.spice.tmpl) measures
*      at, so the decay here is directly comparable to that measurement.
*      V(sn) decays; the driver finds when it has fallen by the labelled
*      sense margin.
*
* SUBSTITUTED BY sim/bitcell-transient/run_bitcell_transient.py:
*   @@PDK_NGSPICE_LIB@@  the shipped sky130 combined model library (the
*                        ONLY PDK file this deck references -- no local
*                        model edits)
*   @@CORNER@@           tt|ss|ff|sf|fs   (the 5 shipped MOS corners)
*   @@TEMP_C@@           -40|27|125       (the adopted temperature grid)
*   @@DESIGN_NETLIST@@   absolute path to design/gain_cell_2t.spice
*   @@C_SN_F@@           lumped storage-node capacitance, in farads
*   @@VRBL@@             read-bitline bias, in volts
*   @@VBL_DATA@@         bitline level during the write pulse (VDD => write
*                        '1', 0 => write '0')
*   @@VSN_INIT@@         storage-node initial condition (.ic)
*   @@TSTEP@@ @@TSTOP@@ @@TMAX@@   .tran arguments
*   @@OUT@@              wrdata output path
*
* The .param block below is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the phase
* timing and the supply/bias levels: run_bitcell_transient.py parses these
* exact lines out of this template and uses them as its measurement
* instants, so the deck's waveform and the driver's sampling points cannot
* drift apart.

.param VDD    = 1.8
.param VRBL   = @@VRBL@@

.param TEDGE       = 100p
.param TWL_ON      = 1n
.param TWL_OFF     = 21n
.param TBL_OFF     = 23n
.param TRWL_ON     = 30n
.param TRWL_OFF    = 50n
.param THOLD_START = 55n

.param VBL_DATA = @@VBL_DATA@@
.param VSN_INIT = @@VSN_INIT@@

.lib "@@PDK_NGSPICE_LIB@@" @@CORNER@@

.temp @@TEMP_C@@

.include @@DESIGN_NETLIST@@

* Lumped storage-node capacitance. Default value is the post-layout
* extracted total for `sn` (layout/gain_cell_2t.extract.parasitics.json,
* issue #7); `--c-sn-ff 0` removes it so only the device models' own
* (bias-dependent) capacitance loads the node. See the README's
* "Storage-node capacitance: two bounds, not one number".
c_sn sn 0 @@C_SN_F@@

* Write wordline: one 0 -> VDD -> 0 pulse. PULSE's pw is measured between
* the end of the rise and the start of the fall, hence the -TEDGE term;
* the period is 1 s so the pulse never repeats inside any .tran window.
vwl  wl  0 pulse(0 {VDD} {TWL_ON} {TEDGE} {TEDGE} {TWL_OFF-TWL_ON-TEDGE} 1)

* Write bitline: held at the data level from t=0 through the whole
* wordline pulse, released to 0 at TBL_OFF (after wl is fully low).
vbl  bl  0 pwl(0 {VBL_DATA} {TBL_OFF} {VBL_DATA} {TBL_OFF+TEDGE} 0)

* Read wordline / row source line: idles at VDD (row deselected, M_RD
* off), pulsed LOW between TRWL_ON and TRWL_OFF to select the row.
vrwl rwl 0 pwl(0 {VDD} {TRWL_ON} {VDD} {TRWL_ON+TEDGE} 0 {TRWL_OFF} 0 {TRWL_OFF+TEDGE} {VDD})

* Read bitline held at a fixed bias; this source's branch current is the
* measured read current (negative = current drawn out of rbl into the
* cell, i.e. a stored '1' discharging the read bitline).
vrbl rbl 0 dc {VRBL}

.ic v(sn)={VSN_INIT}

.control
set filetype=ascii
tran @@TSTEP@@ @@TSTOP@@ 0 @@TMAX@@
wrdata @@OUT@@ v(sn) i(vrbl)
.endc

.end
